course: dictionary
lesson: 11107
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is right. The word whine is a good example. Its meaning depends on who or what is making the sound. «Use your words» means stop hitting, screaming or whining and say what you want. Here whining is a complaint.
explain: «No wonder he is whining at his bowl.» Here whine is not a complaint. A hungry dog makes a long, high, sad sound, so this whine is that sound. Always ask: what is making the sound, and why? The answer will show you the meaning.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try «No wonder he is complaining at his bowl»: it sounds odd for a dog, so the animal meaning fits better. Try «the whine of an engine» with «the complaint of an engine»: that does not make sense, so the machine meaning must be right.
fact: Whine can be a verb (to whine) or a noun (a whine).
fact: To whine means to complain in an annoying, high, unhappy voice, often about small things.
fact: A dog whines when it makes a long, high, sad sound, like at the door to go out.
fact: A machine whines when it makes a long, high, steady noise, like «the whine of an engine».
fact: Calling someone «a whiner» is a bit unkind, so think before you say it.
exercise: «No wonder he is whining at his bowl.» What is the dog doing? | *Making a long, high, sad sound | Sleeping peacefully | Barking at a visitor | Eating very fast
exercise: «Stop whining and tell me what you want.» What does whining mean here? | *Complaining in an annoying, high voice | Running away | Singing a happy tune | Laughing loudly
exercise: What does the whine of an engine mean? | A loud crash | A sudden silence | A soft, happy purr | *A long, high, steady noise
test: The dog began to whine at the back door. What does whine mean? | *Make a long, high, sad sound | Clap its paws | Fall fast asleep | Wag its tail for joy
test: Which sentence uses whine as a noun? | She will whine about her homework all evening | *The whine of the drill hurt my ears | The dog will whine all night | They whine when they are tired
exam: Why is calling someone «a whiner» a bit unkind? | It is a type of bird | It makes them laugh | *It labels a person as always complaining | It means they sing very well
